    <tr>
      <td>
<![endif]-->
<div class="abe-section-block" data-block-type="FancyBlockSection" data-block-id="94837429">
  <table class="abe-section-table" width="100%" align="center" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" role="presentation" style="max-width: 600px; -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; border-spacing: 0; mso-table-lspace: 0pt; mso-table-rspace: 0pt;">
    <tr id="abe-section-row-c3addf2f-bfed-4fda-bb1f-150f573f9a31" class="abe-section-row" style="background-color: #FFFFFF;" bgcolor="#FFFFFF">
      <td style="text-align: center; vertical-align: top; font-size: 0; -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; mso-table-lspace: 0pt; mso-table-rspace: 0pt;" align="center" valign="top">
        <!--[if (gte mso 9)|(IE)]>
  <table width="100%" align="center" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; border-spacing: 0; mso-table-lspace: 0pt; mso-table-rspace: 0pt;">
    <tr>
<![endif]-->
<!--[if (gte mso 9)|(IE)]>
  <td width="600" valign="top" id="abe-column-block-91eb05c7-befc-47dc-baec-ba7fa1c44157-outlook-only" class="abe-column-block-outlook-only" style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; mso-table-lspace: 0pt; mso-table-rspace: 0pt;">
<![endif]-->
<div id="abe-column-block-91eb05c7-befc-47dc-baec-ba7fa1c44157" class="abe-column-block" data-block-type="FancyBlockColumn" data-block-id="94837430" style="width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; display: inline-block; font-size: 16px; vertical-align: top;">
  <table width="100%" align="center" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" role="presentation" style="table-layout: fixed; overflow-wrap: break-word; word-wrap: break-word; text-align: left; -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; border-spacing: 0; mso-table-lspace: 0pt; mso-table-rspace: 0pt;">
    <tr>
      <td class="abe-column-block-padding" id="abe-column-block-91eb05c7-befc-47dc-baec-ba7fa1c44157-padding" style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; mso-table-lspace: 0pt; mso-table-rspace: 0pt; padding: 15px;">
<img class="govd_template_image" src="https://content.govdelivery.com/attachments/fancy_images/OHCCC/2023/02/7184314/add-a-subheading-3_original.png" style="width: 570px; height: auto; -ms-interpolation-mode: bicubic; line-height: 1; outline: none; text-decoration: none; max-width: 100%; border: none;" alt="CLose 2" width="570" height="239"><p style="text-align: justify; -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 15px; margin: 1em 0 15px;" align="justify">As a Right of Way Permit recipient, it is required for you to report all lane closures and placement of steel plates quickly and efficiently. That's why we're excited to announce our new on-line reporting system, which is specifically designed to make the process easier and more convenient. This system is available 24/7, so you can report lane closures and steel plates at any time. With the user-friendly interface, you can easily navigate the system and submit your reports in just a few clicks. We believe that this on-line reporting system will streamline the reporting process and ultimately save you both time and hassle. This program also allows City personnel to quickly obtain pertinent information regarding a closure and/or steel plate in the event of an emergency.</p>
<table class="gd_combo_table" width="100%" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; border-spacing: 0; mso-table-lspace: 0pt; mso-table-rspace: 0pt; table-layout: fixed; overflow-wrap: break-word;">
  <tr class="gd_combo_first_image" style="vertical-align: top;">
    <td class="gd_combo_image_cell" width="180" style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; mso-table-lspace: 0pt; mso-table-rspace: 0pt;"><img class="govd_template_image" src="https://content.govdelivery.com/attachments/fancy_images/OHCCC/2023/06/7817531/123_original.jpg" style="width: 180px; height: auto; -ms-interpolation-mode: bicubic; line-height: 1; outline: none; text-decoration: none; max-width: 100%; border: none;" alt="CLOSE NEw" width="180" height="288"></td>
<td class="gd_combo_spacer" width="4" style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; mso-table-lspace: 0pt; mso-table-rspace: 0pt; width: 8px;"></td>
<td class="gd_combo_text_cell" style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; mso-table-lspace: 0pt; mso-table-rspace: 0pt;">
<p style="text-align: left; -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 15px;" align="left"><strong>This program allows for more accurate and expedited entries. Any personnel with internet access should be able to complete a form allowing onsite personnel to complete.</strong></p>
<p style="text-align: left; -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 15px;" align="left">Multiple plates and closure locations can be entered during one survey allowing notifications to be centralized if that if preferred. <strong>The CLOSE web form is found <a href="https://www.columbus.gov/CLOSE?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; color: #1D5782;">HERE</a></strong></p>
<p style="text-align: left; -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 15px;" align="left"><strong>Please see our <a href="https://content.govdelivery.com/attachments/OHCCC/2023/02/21/file_attachments/2415661/CLOSE_TipCard.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; color: #1D5782;">"Tip Card"</a> for further details.</strong></p>
</td>
